 ### IMPORT-025 — Key callout title normalization
 - **Type:** conversion
-- **Trigger:** A callout box's (IMPORT-024) heading text, cleaned and cased, reads exactly "key facts", "key dates" or "application due date". Existing recognition of a matching heading/paragraph immediately before a one-cell table also applies; it remains an ordinary, non-callout heading.
-- **Action:** Retitled to canonical capitalization ("Key facts"/"Key dates"/"Application due date") and forced to `h4`. Keep the supplied deadline title rather than renaming it or synthesizing another box. Preserve date text and links to ordinary Key dates content. New imports and authorized re-imports share this behavior; no saved-record migration or template-date gate. At rendering, named Application due date callouts use the same first-section portrait sidebar as legacy Key dates; their simple date/link body does not receive the legacy colon formatting. Both source boxes, if supplied, remain in source order with no selection or deletion. Plain headings/prose are not floating callouts.
+- **Trigger:** A callout box's (IMPORT-024) heading text, cleaned and cased, reads exactly "key facts", "key dates" or "application due date". Existing recognition of a matching heading/paragraph immediately before a one-cell table also applies; it remains an ordinary, non-callout heading. During Builder import and re-import, a one-cell callout under Step 1: Review the Opportunity → Basic information with no styled heading also qualifies when its first standalone paragraph matches one of the same titles exactly after case and whitespace normalization. Inline emphasis in the label is allowed. Paragraphs elsewhere and multi-cell tables do not qualify for this fallback.
+- **Action:** Move the matching paragraph into the editable subsection title and retain subsequent content and links in the callout body. Matching titles are retitled to canonical capitalization ("Key facts"/"Key dates"/"Application due date") and forced to `h4`. Keep the supplied deadline title rather than renaming it or synthesizing another box. Preserve date text and links to ordinary Key dates content. New imports and authorized re-imports share this behavior; no saved-record migration or template-date gate. At rendering, named Application due date callouts use the same first-section portrait sidebar as legacy Key dates; their simple date/link body does not receive the legacy colon formatting. Both source boxes, if supplied, remain in source order with no selection or deletion. Plain headings/prose are not floating callouts.
 - **Source:** `content_processing.py::get_subsections_from_sections` (`key_callout_titles`)
 - **Status:** active
 
